{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"3a33af34e4d8a7902accddd8202823e2b0ce620ff5465512410b87271857e67b","digest":{"component_or_area":"mapping seam documentation and portability","key_entities":["[tool.rebar.mapping]","docs/config.md","docs/mapping-seam.md","docs/README.md","CHANGELOG","S1–S8","status axis","type axis","link axis","priority axis","create_defaults axis",".bridge_state/projects.json","probe command","breadcrumb","replay","injected-transport tests"],"problem_keywords":["documentation","portability","mapping seam","provider-neutral","migration safety","backward compatibility"],"propositions":["The mapping seam must be documented end-to-end across config reference, seam architecture, and provider-neutral reuse contract to enable future integrations (Linear, GitLab, GitHub-Issues) beyond the current Jira adapter.","The feature must be demonstrably provider-neutral: every mapping behavior is exercised by in-process unit tests with injected transports requiring no live Jira and no specific CI provider, with the probe command degrading offline and never serving as a CI gate.","The mapping seam is additive and backward-compatible: an absent [tool.rebar.mapping] section reproduces current hardcoded behavior exactly, requires no store migration, and can be rolled back by deletion.","Documentation must cover the full axis catalog (status, type, link, priority, create_defaults), three-layer merge semantics, per-project keying, fail-closed validation, and orthogonality to .bridge_state/projects.json."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787570690071067001,"uuid":"17ed57b7-64bb-487d-8c82-384d85c761fc"}